# Prefer MCP for Data-Platform Queries

When querying Snowflake, Salesforce, dbt, or Sigma, **always use the configured MCP servers via `CallMcpTool` first**. Do **not** generate Python scripts that authenticate directly.

Two exceptions where MCP cannot be used:

- **Atlassian (Jira / Confluence)** — MCP server broken; use REST API with `$JIRA_EMAIL` + `$JIRA_TOKEN` from `~/.zshrc` (see Atlassian section).
- **Google Drive / Sheets** — Workday IT has GCP disabled, so no Drive MCP is possible; use Snowflake `BASE_PROD.GOOGLE_SHEETS.*`, public CSV export URLs, manual CSV download, or `cursor-ide-browser` MCP (see Google Drive section).

## The Hard Rule

| Task | DO this | NEVER do this |
|---|---|---|
| Run a Snowflake SQL query | `CallMcpTool` → `project-0-eda-dbt-em-snowflake` → `snowflake_query` | `python3 -c "import snowflake.connector; ... authenticator='externalbrowser'"` |
| Run a Salesforce SOQL query | `CallMcpTool` → `project-0-eda-dbt-em-salesforce` → `run_soql_query` | `simple_salesforce`, `requests` to Salesforce REST, `sf` CLI |
| Run / show / compile a dbt model | `CallMcpTool` → `project-0-eda-dbt-em-dbt` → `run` / `show` / `compile` / `build` | Shell `dbt run` (only allowed if MCP is unavailable AND user explicitly approves) |
| Read a Sigma workbook / element SQL | `CallMcpTool` → `project-0-eda-dbt-em-sigma` → `sigma_*` | Direct Sigma REST API calls in Python |
| Read a Google Sheet (Fivetran-synced) | Snowflake MCP → `BASE_PROD.GOOGLE_SHEETS.<TABLE>` with `LIMIT` for head, `ORDER BY _fivetran_synced DESC LIMIT` for tail | `googleapiclient`, `gspread`, `pydrive`, OAuth Python — GCP is disabled for Workday accounts |
| Read a Google Sheet (NOT in Snowflake, link-viewable) | `curl -sL "https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/{ID}/export?format=csv&gid={GID}"` then `head` / `tail` / `awk` | Setting up gdrive MCP (blocked — no GCP access) |
| Read a private Google Sheet / Doc / Slides | Ask user to download as CSV (or screenshot for Doc/Slides), then read locally with `Read` tool, OR use `cursor-ide-browser` MCP to navigate the doc URL | Any Python Google API library — all require OAuth which the user cannot create |
| Read / update Jira or Confluence | `curl` REST API with `$JIRA_EMAIL` + `$JIRA_TOKEN` from `~/.zshrc` (Atlassian MCP is currently broken) | `CallMcpTool` → Atlassian MCP (do not use until MCP is fixed) |

## Why this rule exists

- MCP servers are **already authenticated** for the user's session. Each call is a sub-second HTTP round trip.
- Generated Python scripts that use `authenticator='externalbrowser'` trigger a fresh SSO browser flow on every invocation. If the user is away from the keyboard, the script hangs for minutes and blocks the agent's terminal.
- Raw Python scripts also lose the typed, schema-aware error messages that MCP returns.
- Direct API scripting accumulates context (long terminal logs) that bloats the conversation transcript and slows future turns.

## Forbidden patterns (do not generate)

```python
# FORBIDDEN — will cause SSO browser hang
import snowflake.connector
conn = snowflake.connector.connect(
    user='...',
    account='...',
    authenticator='externalbrowser',
    ...
)
```

```python
# FORBIDDEN — same SSO problem under simple_salesforce
from simple_salesforce import Salesforce
sf = Salesforce(username='...', password='...', ...)
```

```bash
# FORBIDDEN unless user has explicitly asked for shell-mode execution
dbt run --select my_model
dbt show --inline "select ..."
```

## Google Drive / Sheets — no MCP, use existing channels

Workday corporate Google accounts have GCP disabled, so the official Google Drive MCP cannot be set up. Pick the right channel based on what the sheet/file is:

### Decision tree

```
Sheet/file you need to read
├── Already in Snowflake (BASE_PROD.GOOGLE_SHEETS.*)?    ──► Snowflake MCP (preferred)
├── No, but link-viewable / public?                      ──► curl + CSV export URL
├── Private + small + one-off?                           ──► Ask user to download CSV, read locally
├── Private + need interactive read?                     ──► cursor-ide-browser MCP
└── Will be touched repeatedly?                          ──► File ticket for Fivetran connector
```

### Snowflake MCP for synced sheets (preferred)

```sql
-- list available synced sheets
select table_name, row_count, last_altered
from BASE_PROD.information_schema.tables
where table_schema = 'GOOGLE_SHEETS'
order by last_altered desc;

-- columns of one sheet
select column_name, data_type
from BASE_PROD.information_schema.columns
where table_schema='GOOGLE_SHEETS' and table_name='<TABLE>'
order by ordinal_position;

-- head 5 / tail 5
select * from BASE_PROD.GOOGLE_SHEETS.<TABLE> limit 5;
select * from BASE_PROD.GOOGLE_SHEETS.<TABLE> order by _fivetran_synced desc limit 5;
```

### CSV export URL for link-viewable sheets

```bash
SHEET_ID="<long-id-from-url>"
GID="<tab-id-from-#gid=>"
curl -sL "https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/$SHEET_ID/export?format=csv&gid=$GID" | head -10
curl -sL "https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/$SHEET_ID/export?format=csv&gid=$GID" | tail -10
curl -sL "https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/$SHEET_ID/gviz/tq?tqx=out:csv&sheet=<TabName>" | head -10
```

Returns HTML (not CSV) → sheet is private, fall back to manual-download or browser MCP.

### Manual CSV download for private sheets

Tell the user: *"In Google Sheets, File → Download → Comma-separated values (.csv), save to `~/Downloads/`, then send me the path."* Then read with the `Read` tool.

### Browser MCP for ad-hoc Drive viewing

```
CallMcpTool → cursor-ide-browser → browser_navigate → https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/.../edit
CallMcpTool → cursor-ide-browser → browser_snapshot
CallMcpTool → cursor-ide-browser → browser_take_screenshot
```

Slow for bulk reads; Sheets renders as a canvas so row-level scraping is unreliable. Best for Docs / Slides peek.

### Forbidden Google API libraries

```python
# FORBIDDEN — all require OAuth that user cannot create (GCP disabled by Workday IT)
import googleapiclient
import gspread
import pydrive
from google.oauth2 import service_account
```

If the user asks "can we just use gspread?", remind them GCP is disabled and offer the four channels above.

## Atlassian (Jira / Confluence) — REST API instead of MCP

The Atlassian MCP server is currently unreliable. Use the Jira/Confluence REST API directly via `curl` with credentials sourced from `~/.zshrc`.

### Standard pattern

```bash
source ~/.zshrc 2>/dev/null
curl -s -u "$JIRA_EMAIL:$JIRA_TOKEN" \
  -H "Accept: application/json" \
  "$JIRA_BASE_URL/rest/api/2/issue/EDAEM-1234"
```

### Available environment variables (already set in `~/.zshrc`)

| Variable | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `JIRA_EMAIL` | Atlassian account email (basic auth user) |
| `JIRA_TOKEN` | Atlassian API token (basic auth password) |
| `JIRA_BASE_URL` | e.g. `https://workdaybt.atlassian.net` |
| `JIRA_PROJECT` | Default Jira project key |

### Common Jira REST endpoints

| Action | Method | Endpoint |
|---|---|---|
| Get issue | GET | `/rest/api/2/issue/{key}` |
| Search by JQL | GET | `/rest/api/2/search?jql=<encoded JQL>` |
| Create issue | POST | `/rest/api/2/issue` |
| Add comment | POST | `/rest/api/2/issue/{key}/comment` |
| Transition issue | POST | `/rest/api/2/issue/{key}/transitions` |

### Common Confluence REST endpoints

| Action | Method | Endpoint |
|---|---|---|
| Get page by ID | GET | `/wiki/rest/api/content/{id}?expand=body.storage,version` |
| Search content | GET | `/wiki/rest/api/content/search?cql=<encoded CQL>` |
| Create page | POST | `/wiki/rest/api/content` |
| Update page | PUT | `/wiki/rest/api/content/{id}` |

### Notes

- Use `curl`, not Python `urllib` — sandbox SSL issues with Python.
- Jira API JSON sometimes contains invalid escape sequences; sanitize before `json.loads()` with `re.sub(r'(?<!\\)\\(?!["\\/bfnrtu])', r'\\\\', raw)`.
- Re-source `~/.zshrc` at the start of each shell call (env vars don't persist between sandboxed runs).
- This is the **preferred** path for Atlassian, not a fallback. Do not retry the Atlassian MCP unless the user confirms it has been fixed.

## Approved exceptions for Snowflake / Salesforce / dbt / Sigma

For these four servers (MCP is healthy), you may fall back to direct scripting **only if all three apply**:

1. The MCP server has returned an explicit error (timeout, auth failure, schema error) that cannot be worked around by reformulating the call.
2. The fallback is **transient** for one task — not a new pattern for the session.
3. You **state the fallback reason explicitly** to the user before generating the script, e.g. "MCP `snowflake_query` returned X; falling back to one direct query — will switch back after this."

## Discovering MCP tool schemas

Before any first-time call to an MCP tool, read its descriptor:

```
/Users/<user>/.cursor/projects/<project>/mcps/<server>/tools/<tool>.json
```

This is mandatory per the global `mcp_file_system` rule. It prevents the "invalid identifier" / parameter-mismatch loops that come from guessing the schema.

## Quick column-discovery pattern (instead of trial-and-error)

When you don't know an exact column name, query `information_schema.columns` first via MCP — one call — instead of running a guess-fix-rerun loop on Python scripts:

```sql
select column_name, data_type
from <DB>.information_schema.columns
where table_schema = '<SCHEMA>' and table_name = '<TABLE>'
order by ordinal_position;
```

## Session hygiene that supports this rule

- Long-running `python3 ... <<PY` heredocs writing to a log file are a strong signal you've drifted into the forbidden pattern. Stop and switch to `CallMcpTool`.
- If the user pastes a previous Python+SSO snippet and asks you to "run it", offer to rewrite the SQL as a single `snowflake_query` MCP call first.
- If the user has been waiting >30s for a Snowflake result, never spawn a second concurrent Python+SSO process. Cancel the first, switch to MCP.

## Reference

Per-server config and troubleshooting lives in `~/.cursor/skills/mcp-connections/` and the `.cursor/mcp.json` file in each workspace.
